cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or analysis, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Linux Kernel Vulnerability Insights: 20 Years of Security Bug Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Analysis of 125,000+ Linux kernel bug-fix pairs spanning 2004-2024,
  revealing patterns in vulnerability lifetimes, reviewer effectiveness,
  and subsystem-specific security characteristics. Key findings include
  a 2.1-year median bug lifetime, identification of 117 "super-reviewers"
  who catch bugs 47% faster, and temporal patterns showing weekend commits
  have 45% longer bug survival times.
